  "query_preview": "../ Tuesday through Saturday / Flow pattern aloft \nshifts more zonal headed into midweek that will mean quicker \nsystem transitions. A stronger feature for late Monday to Tuesday\nthen Wednesday. A trailing feature along the boundary will likely\nrun along the feature, and then across the southern panhandle or \ninto British Columbia. Behind that, looks like SEAK may get \nanother break in the weather, that means we are still waiting for \nthe SEAK fall to arrive. \n\nRainfall totals for the Tuesday to Wednesday time frame are\nlooking to be maybe 1.5 to 2.25 inches for the 24 hr and up to\nmaybe 1 inch for the different portion of the panhandle. \n\nPrecipitation will be tapering off Thursday and skies bringing\nmore breaks and what is looking to be start of dry weekend, based\non the current solutions.",
